-- 1176 — CONTRACT phase: drop the superseded TOTAL dedup index on
-- spec_evidence_bindings.
--
-- EI-23634085867209303. Second half of the expand/contract begun in 1175, which
-- created the partial index spec_evidence_bindings_dedup_live (live proof only) and
-- deliberately left the total index spec_evidence_bindings_dedup in place.
--
-- DO NOT ARM THIS UNTIL THE PREDICATED WRITER IS THE DEPLOYED ONE.
--
-- Arming precondition, in full: the release build serving :3070 must carry the
-- `ON CONFLICT (...) WHERE retracted_at IS NULL` form of bindSpecEvidence
-- (packages/operator-core/lib/agent-tools/plans/spec-evidence-store.ts). Until it
-- does, the deployed writer's un-predicated ON CONFLICT has no inferrable arbiter the
-- moment this index is gone, and EVERY spec-evidence insert fails at plan time with
-- 42P10 ("there is no unique or exclusion constraint matching the ON CONFLICT
-- specification") — not only conflicting ones. That is the migration-461/564/689
-- fleet-outage class; 1175's header carries the measured A/B behind this claim.
--
-- Check the precondition before arming (both must hold):
--   1. dev:pipeline_position { path: 'packages/operator-core/lib/agent-tools/plans/spec-evidence-store.ts' }
--      reports serving.startedSinceCodeChange for the predicated-ON-CONFLICT edit;
--   2. the :3070 health sha matches the build that contains it.
--
-- FORWARD-COMPAT: this is destructive DDL (DROP INDEX), and it is held at the .DRAFT
-- path precisely BECAUSE the currently-deployed release still uses the index it drops.
-- It becomes forward-compatible only once the precondition above is satisfied, at
-- which point no deployed code targets spec_evidence_bindings_dedup any more.
--
-- LOCK NOTE (EI-23627339402596541, measured on this exact statement): DROP INDEX needs
-- ACCESS EXCLUSIVE, and every migration runs inside BEGIN/COMMIT so CONCURRENTLY forms
-- are unavailable. A concurrent whole-database dump holding ACCESS SHARE on the table
-- fails this with 55P03 (lock timeout) and aborts operator boot. Arm it when no backup
-- is in flight, and expect a retry to be needed rather than treating 55P03 as a defect
-- in this file.

DROP INDEX IF EXISTS harness_shared.spec_evidence_bindings_dedup;
